#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "0a5391bf-06ef-5099-a835-0375ff96c342" :question/math-academy-id "e-1038" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5x+3y+4 &=0 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5x+3y+4 &=0 && |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe also notice that each equation can be simplified by dividing by a common factor. In the first equation, the common factor is $5,$ while in the second equation, the common factor is $4.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+30y+40 &=0 && |\\,÷5 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20 && |\\,÷4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $x.$ So, we can substitute $x = -5y-5$ into the first equation and then solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+6y+8 & =0 \\\\ (-5y-5)+6y+8 & =0 \\\\ y+3 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-3$ back into $x=-5y-5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-5y-5 \\\\  & =-5(-3)-5 \\\\  & =15-5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 10$ and $y = -3,$ which can be expressed as $(10, -3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096369 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "8f4b321d-ebc7-5f78-9bde-b51b297a0cc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-1039" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1.4x+2.8y &=1.4 \\\\ 0.02x+0.01y &=0.05\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10$ and the second equation by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1.4x+2.8y &=1.4 && |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.02x+0.01y &=0.05 && |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo simplify the first equation, we divide by $14\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}14x+28y &=14 && |÷14 \\\\ 2x+y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =1 \\\\ x & =1-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can substitute $x=1-2y$ into the second equation and then solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =5 \\\\ 2(1-2y)+y & =5 \\\\ 2-4y+y & =5 \\\\ 2-3y & =5 \\\\ -3y & =3 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ back into $x=1-2y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1-2y \\\\  & =1-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x =3$ and $y =-1$, which can be expressed as $(3, -1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18379570-3573-56f1-ab2f-409230c665e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285002} {:answer/id #uuid "2048a0a2-d38b-500f-b1cf-d208a4910fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285079} {:answer/id #uuid "33624308-466d-5a86-b996-91ff0395f5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285256} {:answer/id #uuid "49c9eb6f-216d-5f7c-b9c2-9868dccfc81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285469} {:answer/id #uuid "d6430e16-c3e1-5238-9e78-0f4ef31b5445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18379570-3573-56f1-ab2f-409230c665e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285002} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3a2076-6fe5-5f27-acde-2eb1abd84aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "156c3b0d-28fb-58f6-9d7c-fb391142fe01" :question/math-academy-id "q-18702" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x-y?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y &=69 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y &=69 && |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y &=690 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the first equation by $23$ and the second equation by $10,$ we will get a $2y$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-2y$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y &=690 && |\\,÷23 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100 && |\\,÷10\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=30 \\\\ x-2y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\cancel{2y} & =30 \\\\ x-\\cancel{2y} & =10 \\\\ (x+x) & =(30+10) \\\\ 2x & =40 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=20$ into the equation $x+2y=30$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =30 \\\\ (20)+2y & =30 \\\\ 2y & =30-20 \\\\ 2y & =10 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=20$ and $y=5.$ So, \n\n$$\nx-y=20-(5)=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ba4e4e-fd4a-5581-8c4f-f4840ad3239c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4.75, q = 5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094868} {:answer/id #uuid "e4caf298-41f2-5f35-96c0-264d9278d70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 3.5, q = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094869} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b86a7c-97ca-5fa7-9315-0a49c6c37381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 2.25, q = 0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094870} {:answer/id #uuid "1327ea0a-9c1d-5435-8b82-2aa62fc86f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 1.25, q =-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094871} {:answer/id #uuid "21aadab0-c32b-5ed5-a5cb-57f375a27077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 6.5, q = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094872}] :answer-field/id #uuid "92d9c867-3aea-504b-83f3-0aeca8e42f08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094867}] :question/id #uuid "3cdb6891-b142-501a-b07a-0a0cfaa8a9db" :question/math-academy-id "q-18823" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n${0.2p + 0.3q = 0.6; 0.2p - 0.1q = 0.4$"}]}
